# Ham Radio Band Plans

Common amateur radio band frequencies for quick reference.
Use these frequencies with the --frequency option.

## HF Bands (Shortwave)

| Band | Frequency Range (MHz) | Common Modes | Notes |
|------|----------------------|--------------|-------|
| 160m | 1.8 - 2.0 | CW, SSB | Night time DX |
| 80m | 3.5 - 4.0 | CW, SSB, Digital | Good for regional contacts |
| 60m | 5.25 - 5.45 | USB only | Channelized in some regions |
| 40m | 7.0 - 7.3 | CW, SSB, Digital | Popular DX band |
| 30m | 10.1 - 10.15 | CW, Digital only | No voice, narrow band |
| 20m | 14.0 - 14.35 | CW, SSB, Digital | Best all-around DX band |
| 17m | 18.068 - 18.168 | CW, SSB, Digital | Similar to 20m |
| 15m | 21.0 - 21.45 | CW, SSB, Digital | Good during solar max |
| 12m | 24.89 - 24.99 | CW, SSB, Digital | Seasonal DX |
| 10m | 28.0 - 29.7 | CW, SSB, FM, AM | Wide open during solar max |

## VHF/UHF Bands

| Band | Frequency Range (MHz) | Common Modes | Notes |
|------|----------------------|--------------|-------|
| 6m | 50 - 54 | SSB, CW, FM | "Magic band" - sporadic E |
| 2m | 144 - 148 | FM, SSB, CW, Digital | Local repeaters |
| 70cm | 420 - 450 | FM, Digital | Repeaters, satellites |

## Quick Start Frequencies

### SSB (Voice)
- 40m: 7.150 MHz (day), 7.250 MHz (night)
- 20m: 14.200 MHz
- 15m: 21.300 MHz

### CW (Morse Code)
- 40m: 7.050 MHz
- 20m: 14.050 MHz
- 15m: 21.050 MHz

### Digital Modes (FT8, etc.)
- 40m: 7.074 MHz (FT8)
- 20m: 14.074 MHz (FT8)
- 15m: 21.074 MHz (FT8)

## Example Commands

```bash
# Listen to 20m SSB
python src/main.py --frequency 14200000 --gain 30.0

# Listen to 40m FT8 digital
python src/main.py --frequency 7074000 --gain 25.0

# Listen to 2m FM repeater
python src/main.py --frequency 146520000 --sample_rate 192000
```

## Band Conditions

Band propagation varies with:
- Time of day (lower bands better at night)
- Season (summer vs winter)
- Solar cycle (11-year sunspot cycle)
- Solar flux and A/K indices

Check propagation resources:
- [propagation.kc2g.com](https://propagation.kc2g.com/)
- [hamqsl.com/solar.html](https://www.hamqsl.com/solar.html)
